What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/<dev>/rotation
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RW) How far the device is turned from its natural
		orientation, in degrees counter-clockwise: 0, 90, 180 or 270.
		The touch controller firmware places its edge and palm
		rejection zones along the edges the user holds in that
		orientation. Defaults to 0 and is re-applied whenever the
		firmware is reloaded (power cycle, watchdog recovery).

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/<dev>/pen_mode
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RW) 1 to make the controller scan for an active pen, 0 to scan
		for fingers only. Present only when the device tree enables
		pen support. Kept across firmware reloads.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/<dev>/pen_battery
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO) Battery level byte from the pen's last report, -1 before
		any pen report. Present only when the device tree enables pen
		support.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/<dev>/palm_mode
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RW) How hard the controller firmware rejects palm contacts:
		"normal" (default), "enhance" (stronger, for writing with a
		pen while resting a hand on the screen) or "off" (no palm
		rejection, for games with many large contacts). Re-applied
		whenever the firmware is reloaded.

What:		/sys/bus/spi/devices/<dev>/stylus_state
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-input@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		(RO) The controller firmware's pen state from its last report:
		0 left pen mode, 1 pen detected (the firmware waits for the
		display to switch to the refresh rate it scans the pen at),
		2 entered pen mode, -1 before any report. Supports poll().
		Present only when the device tree enables pen support.
